<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρφρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>haughty, arrogant,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆμα, λόγοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				387
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				410
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρονήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					388
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρφρονα</span> as
				Adv., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1236
			</span></i>. Regul. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερφρόνως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					37.5
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				49
			</span></i> (this Adv. is censured by <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				9.147
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in good
			sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ ὑπέρφρονος</span> from
				<i>a sense of superiority,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				45.43
			</span></i>.</div>
